  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "In general the ionic radius increases on moving from top to bottom in group and decreases on moving from left to right in period. So, Na<sup>+</sup>&nbsp;&gt; Li<sup>+</sup>&nbsp;and Mg<sup>2+</sup>&nbsp;&gt; Be<sup>2+</sup>.&nbsp;<br /><br />The size of Mg<sup>2+</sup>&nbsp;is however smaller than Li<sup>+</sup>. Despite the Mg atom having a slightly larger atomic size, the Mg<sup>2+</sup> ion is marginally smaller in size than the Li<sup>+</sup> ion because of its higher nuclear charge<br /><br />Hence, the correct trend is<br /><br /><math><mtext>N</mtext><msubsup><mrow><mtext>a</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>0.98</mn><mtext>Å</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mtext>L</mtext><msubsup><mrow><mtext>i</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>0.68</mn><mtext>Å</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mtext>M</mtext><msubsup><mrow><mtext>g</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>0.65</mn><mtext>Å</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mtext>B</mtext><msubsup><mrow><mtext>e</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>0.62</mn><mtext>Å</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msubsup></math>",
